{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস [স্বাস্থ্য] - মেডিকেল অংশ ": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the following is included in Pharmacokinetics?", "option1": "Receptor interaction", "option2": "Drug absorption", "option3": "Drug antagonism", "option4": "Signal transduction", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Pharmacokinetics(What the body does to a drug): It includes four distinct phases-<br>A.absorption<br>B.distribution<br>C.biotransformation,<br>D.elimination <br> </p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Most drugs are absorbed by-", "option1": "Simple Diffusion", "option2": "facilitated duffusion", "option3": "Active transport", "option4": "Pinocytosis", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_2_HXy72rr.png\" width=\"500\" height=\"660\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which Drug is absorbed by pinocytosis?", "option1": "Levodopa", "option2": "Aspirin", "option3": "Morphine", "option4": "Insulin", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_2_jiLKg3t.png\" width=\"400\" height=\"528\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which drug has a high Vd?", "option1": "Digoxin", "option2": "Gentamicin", "option3": "Amoxicillin", "option4": "Aspirin", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_5_nT5qetA.png\" width=\"400\" height=\"542\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) The principle site of biotransformation is-", "option1": "kidney", "option2": "liver", "option3": "skin", "option4": "brain", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_6_B2sfyeP.png\" width=\"400\" height=\"555\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) The mainn purpose of biotransformation is to:", "option1": "Increase lipid solubility", "option2": "form poler metabolites for excretion", "option3": "increase protien binding capacity", "option4": "increase drug potency", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_6_dB5Tulx.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"416\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) In biotransformation which is a phase-1 reaction?", "option1": "Gluvoronidation", "option2": "Acetylation", "option3": "Oxidation", "option4": "Sulfation", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_8.png\" width=\"500\" height=\"625\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) In First order kinetics, the rate of elimination  of drug is:", "option1": "Zero", "option2": "Constant", "option3": "Proportional ", "option4": "No related with concentration", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2026-07-19_195715.png\" width=\"481\" height=\"273\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which drug follows zero order kinetics?", "option1": "Alchohol", "option2": "Carbamazepine", "option3": "Phenobarbitone", "option4": "Low-dose aspirin", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2026-07-19_195715_uBvx9cj.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"170\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Type A ADRs are usually:", "option1": "Unpredictable", "option2": "Rare", "option3": "Dose related", "option4": "Irreversible", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_11.png\" width=\"400\" height=\"265\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which route bypasses first-pass metabolism?", "option1": "Oral", "option2": "Rectal", "option3": "Sublingual", "option4": "Intragastric", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2026-06-18_174755.png\" width=\"223\" height=\"315\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which one is a G-protien couple receptor?", "option1": "Insulin receptor", "option2": "Beta-adrenoreceptor", "option3": "steroid receptor", "option4": "Nicotinic receptor", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2026-06-18_175302_7M7KTAG.png\" width=\"471\" height=\"139\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Insulin act mainly through ?", "option1": "Ligand-gated ion channels ", "option2": "protien kinase receptor", "option3": "cytosolic receptor", "option4": "Gaba receptor", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_12.png\" width=\"350\" height=\"579\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which is an example of physiological antagonism?", "option1": "Atrophine + Acetylcholine", "option2": "Histamin + Adrenalin", "option3": "Morphine + Naloxone", "option4": "Antacid + HCL", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_13.png\" width=\"350\" height=\"380\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Steady-state concentration is achieved when-", "option1": "Absorption equals distribution", "option2": "Drug administration equals elimination", "option3": "Metabolism equals absorption", "option4": "Metabolism proportional to bioavailability", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_14_9o64R89.png\" width=\"350\" height=\"525\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Partial agonist possesses:", "option1": "affinity without efficacy", "option2": "efficacy but reduced affinity", "option3": "efficacy without affinity", "option4": "affinity but reduced efficacy", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2026-06-18_180325.png\" width=\"471\" height=\"196\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) A drug with a half-life of 1 hour reaches near steady state in-", "option1": "2-3 hours", "option2": "3-4 hours", "option3": "4-5 hourrs", "option4": "5-6 hours", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/new_14.png\" width=\"350\" height=\"525\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Hyperuricemia commonly caused by:", "option1": "Rifampicin", "option2": "Ethambutol", "option3": "Isoniazid", "option4": "Pyrazinamide", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2026-06-18_182855.png\" width=\"469\" height=\"217\" alt=\"\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) ", "opti